    family: "expos",
    rationale: "Advanced (see notes on the swap with the control). v4.4 answers cultural questions in a fixed template: 'ọgbọgaga' 27 times in its 249 train answers against 4 in the 501 gold rows on the same prompts (recount on v44-vs-gold.json); on ig_bank_cult_014 it wrote six sentences (75 words), five of them opening with the habitual 'Amọnẹ a' or 'Ma a', and ended on the unverified gift. Speakers given a bounded question open with the scene: annotator_7 on ig_bank_cult_024 'Chẹñwu ki ọnọnọjọ lọ tu [house] ẹnẹ Igala, ma gbi ọnọnọjọ lẹ kpai [hand] mẹji' against v4.4 'Ọjanẹ Ígáláà, ẹchẹdọ ọnọnọjọ chi ẹñwu ki ñyọ ñyọ'ñyọ i chẹ'; annotator_7 wrote eleven words on pottery (ig_bank_cult_025) where v4.4 wrote 47. The open condolence essay (ig_bank_cult_014) drew a 198-word gold that cannot be compared with anything; fixing the asker (the speaker's own son, on the path) and capping at two sentences makes opener, length and linkers scorable. Score: sentence count, importance opener, 'Àmí' or English inside the Igala (v4.4 'Àmí', ig_bank_auth_033; 'Ẹgba chi ọla ñwu stretch of time', ig_v42_lex_025), and whether the condolence words match the converged gold. Not a control. Final gate: the drafted note, with its speaker forms, is kept verbatim in bank-final-original-notes.json; it left expectedCulturalContext because the seeder leak-checks that field and factual buckets show it to annotators.",
