    difficultyLevel: "basic",
    expectedCulturalContext: "We hold no rule on: the written shape of the negative nasal (six speakers wrote it six ways on ig_bank_gram_019, recorded per speaker and never corrected); which yes-no particle closes the question (several are attested, and sometimes none); whether a main-clause negative takes a preverbal element for some speakers (one speaker's sentences hint at it); whether the be-located verb changes under negation. The three lines give one statement, negative and question set for a third-person singular locative, with the speaker's nasal and particle side by side.",
