    rationale: "Design note (kept from the draft): We hold no rule on whether the progressive question keeps the incompletive a, on whether the third-person plural ma and any negator stack (one ma or two), on whether 'dance' is one verb or a verb plus a noun so that the nasal lands after the noun, or on the particle. The three lines tell us whether the incompletive survives in the affirmative and the question and drops only in the negative, which is the contrast v4.4 gets wrong. Template A, present progressive, third person plural. Within the triplet the affirmative progressive is the control for the negative: it should keep the incompletive the negative drops. Measured failure: for 'They are not eating' all seven speakers drop the incompletive (Ma jẹñwu-n annotator_6, Ma jẹñwu’ñ annotator_5, Mà jẹñwu ǹ annotator_3, Ma jẹnwu nọ annotator_7, Mà jẹnwu nóò annotator_8, Ma jẹ'ñwu no annotator_4, ig_bank_gram_019) while v4.4 keeps it ('Ma á j'ẹñwu ñ'), following its served line that á marks is-doing. This prompt repeats the contrast on a new verb with the progressive affirmative and question beside it, so the á deletion is measured as a paradigm and not as one memorised sentence. Verbs already used by the aspect ladders (wash, sweep, fetch, cook) and by ig_bank_gram_019 (eat) are avoided, and the scene keeps clear of the frozen festival prompt ig_cult_001. Routing: annotator_3 and annotator_5 (the two who write corrected forms with reasons) plus annotators 4, 6, 7 and 8, so every speaker's own nasal shape is recorded. Tag: record-ready (the gold is short spoken lines).",
